    "id": "ser-estar",
    "title": "Ser vs. Estar",
    "text": "Both mean **to be**, but they are not interchangeable.\n\n**SER** = permanent / essential: identity, origin, time, possession, material.\n- *Soy estudiante.* · *Es de México.* · *Son las tres.* · *Es mi libro.*\n\n**ESTAR** = temporary / state / location.\n- *Estoy cansado.* · *Está en casa.* · *Estoy estudiando.*\n\nMnemonic: **\"For how you feel or where you are, always use the verb estar.\"**\nSome adjectives change meaning: *ser listo* (clever) vs *estar listo* (ready); *ser aburrido* (boring) vs *estar aburrido* (bored).",
