  {
    "id": "hay-estar",
    "title": "Hay vs. Está / Están",
    "text": "**hay** = \"there is / there are\" — existence, unspecified things. It never changes.\n**está / están** = \"is / are located\" — a specific, known thing.\n\n- *Hay un banco en la calle.* (There is a bank on the street — any bank)\n- *El banco está en la calle Mayor.* (The bank is on Main Street — that specific bank)\n\nQuestions about existence use **hay**: *¿Hay un hospital aquí?*\nLocation of the known object uses **estar**: *¿Dónde está el hospital?*",
    "table": [
      [
        "Use",
        "Form",
        "Example"
      ],
      [
        "existence",
        "hay",
        "Hay dos libros en la mesa"
      ],
