    "text": "The most common way to talk about the near future: **ir** + **a** + **infinitive**.\n\n- *Voy a estudiar.* — I am going to study.\n- *¿Qué vas a hacer?* — What are you going to do?\n- *Vamos a comer paella.* — We are going to eat paella.\n\nOnly **ir** is conjugated; the second verb stays in the infinitive.\nFor a promise/prediction you can also use the simple future (add endings to the infinitive: hablaré, comerás, vivirá...).",
